Subject: Build the Arm Neon SIMD extensions on x86-64 with SIMDe
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Applies-After: ports/patch/libjpeg-turbo-3.0.1.patch

The x86-64 SIMD extensions are NASM assembly, which Fil-C cannot compile.
The Arm Neon extensions are C intrinsics. With -DSIMDE_NEON=1 they are built
on x86-64 against SIMDe, which maps each Neon intrinsic to SSE intrinsics that
Fil-C compiles and bounds-checks. simd/arm/simde-neon/arm_neon.h replaces the
SIMDe intrinsics that are implemented as element loops and appear in hot
kernels (interleaved loads and stores, transposes, widening shifts, doubling
multiplies) with SSE2 or SSSE3 versions.

The Arm sources test __aarch64__ to mean that size_t and the Huffman bit
buffer are 64 bits wide, so SIMDE_NEON builds take those branches too. The
32-bit branch of jsimd_encode_mcu_AC_refine_prepare_neon writes four size_t
words into a two-word array; Fil-C stopped it.

